{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/025-fancy-fly-boxes/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Wood Times"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"d4c72e7f-eab6-53c6-8bdb-03c2eaea7fad","excerpt":"Fly fishing and woodworking share a certain meditative quality - patience, attention to detail, appreciation for natural materials. I wanted to make some fly…","html":"<p>Fly fishing and woodworking share a certain meditative quality - patience, attention to detail, appreciation for natural materials. I wanted to make some fly boxes for my brothers shop for Christmas.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/a878e/router_jig.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Router Jig\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/f058b/router_jig.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/c26ae/router_jig.png 158w,\n/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/6bdcf/router_jig.png 315w,\n/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/f058b/router_jig.png 630w,\n/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/40601/router_jig.png 945w,\n/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/78612/router_jig.png 1260w,\n/static/1b7ebcefe2a83f9280b75f4d0acc98ce/a878e/router_jig.png 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>A custom router jig ensured consistent pocket depths for the fly foam inserts. The boxes needed to be thin enough to fit in a vest pocket but sturdy enough to protect delicate flies.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/a878e/lid_blanks.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Lid Blanks\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/f058b/lid_blanks.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/c26ae/lid_blanks.png 158w,\n/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/6bdcf/lid_blanks.png 315w,\n/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/f058b/lid_blanks.png 630w,\n/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/40601/lid_blanks.png 945w,\n/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/78612/lid_blanks.png 1260w,\n/static/afefac59817e9e8d090a4bdd3fe3039f/a878e/lid_blanks.png 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>The lids were where the magic happened. Walnut pieces with natural voids and live edges became canvases for epoxy river pours. Each crack and void was an opportunity for color.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/a878e/epoxy_lids.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Epoxy Lids\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/f058b/epoxy_lids.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/c26ae/epoxy_lids.png 158w,\n/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/6bdcf/epoxy_lids.png 315w,\n/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/f058b/epoxy_lids.png 630w,\n/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/40601/epoxy_lids.png 945w,\n/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/78612/epoxy_lids.png 1260w,\n/static/8d74e1a80b8cbb58d9eae2c7785bf2f6/a878e/epoxy_lids.png 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Three lids showing the river table technique at miniature scale. Blue, green, and clear epoxy filled the natural voids in the walnut, creating unique patterns on each box. No two would ever be alike.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/a878e/collection.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Collection\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/f058b/collection.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/c26ae/collection.png 158w,\n/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/6bdcf/collection.png 315w,\n/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/f058b/collection.png 630w,\n/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/40601/collection.png 945w,\n/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/78612/collection.png 1260w,\n/static/e594ed934d8290364ba7b993b2a171f8/a878e/collection.png 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>A batch of boxes ready for finishing. Some with dramatic epoxy rivers, others showcasing figured maple or clean walnut. Variety was the point - every angler has different taste.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/a878e/finished_open.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Finished Open\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/f058b/finished_open.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/c26ae/finished_open.png 158w,\n/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/6bdcf/finished_open.png 315w,\n/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/f058b/finished_open.png 630w,\n/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/40601/finished_open.png 945w,\n/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/78612/finished_open.png 1260w,\n/static/96762d1467acfb7d567cbe010850463c/a878e/finished_open.png 2048w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>The finished product: a walnut box with epoxy accents, brass hinges, and slit foam ready to hold flies. Magnetic closure keeps everything secure while wading in a river.  A few of the boxes has the epoxy surface gouged to look like rippling water.</p>\n<p>These boxes found their way to my brothers and gifts for their customers. Functional art that goes on adventures - getting wet, holding flies, developing patina over years of use. That’s the kind of woodworking that feels meaningful.s</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"Fancy Fly Boxes","date":"November 10, 2019","description":null}},"previous":{"fields":{"slug":"/024-wood-cookie-table/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Wood Cookie Table"}},"next":null},"pageContext":{"id":"d4c72e7f-eab6-53c6-8bdb-03c2eaea7fad","previousPostId":"27e0765e-6657-5ca4-913c-71be8ef0e6b4","nextPostId":null}},"staticQueryHashes":["2841359383"],"slicesMap":{}}